{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Sheol</b> — which is her house. \"They go down\" [refers to] the ways that bring her down, as in the interpretation of \"her paths wander\" [Proverbs 5:6]. Or \"they go down\" is an allusion to her feet. And just as he spoke of the disgrace of the woman, he showed something of the virtue of wisdom, for it disciplines the fools."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:22.630918961Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}